Z||000005||tgowens||11-15-2001||10:29 PM||||Normally, when the engine is top dead center the rotor should point to the 8mm bolt on the plenum - that will be #1 on your dist. cap when you put it on. The routing follows (as JohnF said) 1-2-3-4-5-6  and goes in a clockwise direction. This being said, #1 is closest to the 8mm bolt and routs to #1 plug which is the passenger side of the car on the rear...... next is #2 and goes to passenger side front of the car..... #3 in the middle rear, #4 in the middle front, #5 driver's side rear, and #6 driver's side front......<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
